---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`How ${site.name} collects, uses, discloses and protects personal information, including California (CCPA/CPRA) and multi-state privacy rights.`}
>
  <p>
    {site.name} ("we," "us," or "our") operates this website (the "Site"). This Privacy Policy
    explains what personal information we collect, how we use and disclose it, and the rights you
    may have. Please read it carefully.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
  <h3>Information you give us</h3>
  <p>When you call us, email us, or otherwise communicate with us, we may collect:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Name and contact details (email address, telephone number)</li>
    <li>Details about a vehicle you own or are interested in — make, model, year, VIN, mileage, service history</li>
    <li>The content of your messages and records of our correspondence</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
  <p>
    When you visit the Site, our hosting provider may automatically log technical information such
    as your IP address, browser type and version, operating system, device type, the pages you
    viewed, the date and time of your visit, and the referring URL. We use this information for
    security, troubleshooting, and aggregate traffic analysis.
  </p>

  <div class="note">
    <p>
      <strong>We do not collect payment card numbers, Social Security numbers, or driver's licence
      numbers through this Site.</strong> Vehicle purchases and service payments are handled in person
      or through separate, secured systems.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Respond to inquiries and provide quotes, availability, or appointments</li>
    <li>Schedule, perform, and document vehicle service</li>
    <li>Process and administer a vehicle purchase you request</li>
    <li>Communicate with you about your vehicle, request, or transaction</li>
    <li>Maintain business records and comply with legal, tax, and regulatory obligations</li>
    <li>Detect and prevent fraud, and keep the Site secure</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. How We Share Your Information</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>We do not sell your personal information.</strong> We may disclose it in the following
    limited circumstances:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Service providers</strong> that perform services on our behalf (website hosting, IT
      support, email), bound by confidentiality obligations
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Transaction parties</strong> — lenders, insurers, or title and registration agents —
      where necessary to complete a transaction you requested
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Legal requirements</strong> — government agencies, law enforcement, or other parties
      where required by law, subpoena, or legal process
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Business transfers</strong> — a successor entity in the event of a merger,
      acquisition, or sale of assets
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Cookies and Tracking</h2>
  <p>
    The Site does not use advertising cookies, tracking pixels, or third-party analytics services.
    For details, see our <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Your Privacy Rights</h2>
  <h3>California residents (CCPA/CPRA)</h3>
  <p>If you are a California resident, you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Know what categories and specific pieces of personal information we collect, use, and disclose</li>
    <li>Request deletion of personal information we have collected from you</li>
    <li>Request correction of inaccurate personal information</li>
    <li>Opt out of the sale or sharing of personal information</li>
    <li>Limit the use and disclosure of sensitive personal information</li>
    <li>Not be discriminated against for exercising any of these rights</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not sell or share personal information as those terms are defined by the CCPA. See also
    <a href="/do-not-sell">Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information</a>.
  </p>

  <h3>Residents of other states</h3>
  <p>
    Residents of Virginia, Colorado, Connecticut, Utah, Texas, Oregon, Montana, and other states
    with comprehensive consumer privacy laws may have similar rights, including rights to access,
    correct, delete, obtain a copy of, and opt out of targeted advertising or profiling. To exercise
    any right, contact us using the details below. We will verify your request and respond within
    the time required by applicable law.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Data Retention</h2>
  <p>
    We keep personal information only as long as necessary for the purposes described in this
    policy, and as long as required by law — for example, records relating to vehicle sales,
    service history, and tax obligations.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Security</h2>
  <p>
    We use reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards designed to protect
    personal information. No method of transmission over the internet or method of electronic
    storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Children's Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    The Site is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal
    information from children under 13. If you believe a child has provided us with personal
    information, please contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Third-Party Links</h2>
  <p>
    The Site may link to third-party websites, including vehicle history providers. We are not
    responsible for the privacy practices or content of those sites.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will revise the "Last
    updated" date above. Material changes will be highlighted on this page.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Contact Us</h2>
  <p>
    {site.name}<br />
    {site.address}<br />
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a><br />
    Phone: <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a>
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
